-- Source module: Solutions.KFNIL
/-!
# KFN: implementations by item-language programs

The row additions of Lemma 13 are item-language programs (`IStmt HS 1` calling the Lemma 12
routines under a fixed `iprog`), whose code depends on the input width `w`.  This file gives the
`IStmt` versions of the implementation predicates, with **code families `ℕ → IStmt HS Pp`**
indexed by the input width, run under a fixed `I`, `iprog`:

* `SImplI I iprog r st n T code e dw cost`, `RImplI ...` (as `SImpl`, `RImpl`, with
  `IRuns I iprog (code w)` in place of `FSp code`);
* lifts of the register-program versions (`SImpl.toI`, `RImpl.toI`, via `FSp.irun`);
* `SImplI.comp`, `RImplI.comp`, `rImplI_list`, `sImplI_of_rImplI_roleDiag`, `rImplI_onRole`.
-/

set_option linter.unusedSimpArgs false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

namespace NLogN.KFN

