/-!
# KFN: the phase pass as a selected-bit operator

For selected bits `i : ι` at record strides `2^{pos i} · S` (`pos i < t`) on `B · 2^t · S`
records of `r` entries, the phase pass `phL (S r) t B u (aEof pos a')` implements the diagonal
`x ↦ i^{u + Σ_i a'_i x_i}` (**`sImpl_phase`**), exactly (no scale, no width change), at cost
`cPhL`, linear in the data.
